Vermintide is my favorite game to play after a hard day, beating hordes of
Skavens to a pulp is weirdly relaxing for me (
).
This game is also a great way to immerse yourself in the Warhammer fantasy world. It's thrilling to be able to experience the old world in first person. The End Times setting adds a sense of impending doom, that really immerse yourself in the world and inspire you to fight for it's survival. (
)
Gameplay wise, each weapon is easy to use but difficult to master (
) they all have their strengths and weaknesses, for example:
You will need to play cooperatively to survive the Skaven horde, especially the special ones (
)
Completing the missions on the hardest difficulties is really statisfying.
The loot system in this game is a bit controversial but I like it. At the end of any mission you throw a set of dice in hope to get the best roll and thus the best gear. However you can significantly increase your chances of a good roll by finding hidden tomes and grimoires within the level (
). If you're lucky you can also encounter a sack rat or loot additional dice in chests. (
)
The game has its flaws however:
I would recommend you to play this game with a group of friends (
) as playing with random players can sometimes be nerve-racking as you can't survive in this game if you do not play cooperatively (
).
