That's the case when you need neutral rating for the review, not only "recommend", "not recommend". It's not a bad game, but there are a lot of cons. If you want to play it, be ready for:
- dull, uninteresting, sometimes really dumb characters;
- incoherent storyline;
- not understanding what da hell is going on until you play all the DLCs;
- tons and TONS of blood and gore.
My favorite moment: 1/3 of the game is behind, main character, Sebastian, after one more horrifying scene utter with completely emotionless voice to the companion "Let's just get out of here, there is something wrong with this place." Well, well, well, our detective started to suspect something at last! xD
But still, there are positive moments too: upgrade system, exploring, seeking for secrets, not trivial boss fights...
I would rate it 5.5 out of 10. Buy it only if you like horrors and only when the game and season pass are on sale.

